  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Is aviation a good career in India? Yes, for some doors and not for others, and the door you choose matters more than the word aviation.</strong>
    Cabin crew, air traffic control and pilot careers are gated and rank-bound. Aircraft maintenance and drone work have more room to grow into services of your own.
    The people who come out ahead check the age, medical and money rules first, then build a <strong>high-value skill portfolio</strong> that works even if one airline stops hiring. Those are the decisions that unlock high income opportunities and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Aviation is eight different careers. Airports handled 412 million passengers in FY25, so demand is real, but each door has its own age, medical and licence gate.</li>
      <li><strong>Lead with the doors that scale: drone services and aircraft maintenance. Cabin crew, ATC, ground jobs and pilot are salaried ladders with a short or narrow top, so plan the exit early.</strong></li>
      <li>Airlines train their own crew and charge no placement fee. Pay for a licence course only when the law needs it, and keep any education spend near 10% of your budget.</li>
      <li>Next step: pick one door from the table, run the free check for it (medical, notice, rules), then talk to three people doing the job.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

