  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer to "is aviation a good career"</h2>

  <p>
    "Aviation" is a sector, not a job. A cabin crew member, an aircraft engineer, an air traffic controller, a ground officer, a drone operator and a pilot have different entry exams, different regulators and very different long-term income.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is why the honest answer splits. The sector is growing and the work is real. But the best-known doors, the uniform ones, are also the ones with age caps, fitness checks and small ladders.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Most social posts about an air hostess or pilot career show the uniform and skip the entry rules, the shift pattern and the exit plan. The more useful question is not "is aviation good" but "which door fits my body, my stream, my money and my plan for year five".
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="demand">Is the sector growing, and who gets hired</h2>

  <p>
    Growth is real, but it comes in waves. These are the signals we could source, with what each one means for someone starting out.
